{#-
  What a segment of an actor's chat opens with (procreator/actor.ts): the story as far as it
  shapes them (its title, how dark it goes, the world), who they are, and after a compaction what
  they remember of the chat before, in their own voice. It stays word for word the same through
  its segment, so every call can be cached. Takes an ActorHeadView (story/view.ts).
-#}
<story title="{{ title }}">
How dark: {{ darkness }}
</story>
{% if world.genre or world.tone or world.setting or world.rules or world.notes %}

<world>
{% if world.genre %}
Genre: {{ world.genre }}
{% endif %}
{% if world.tone %}
Tone: {{ world.tone }}
{% endif %}
{% if world.setting %}
Setting: {{ world.setting }}
{% endif %}
{% if world.rules %}
Rules: {{ world.rules }}
{% endif %}
{% if world.notes %}
Notes: {{ world.notes }}
{% endif %}
</world>
{% endif %}

{{ self }}
{% if memory %}

<what_you_remember>
{{ memory }}
</what_you_remember>
The chat goes on from here, word for word.
{% endif %}
